@startuml
' Purpose: Case lifecycle states and transitions
' Source of truth:
'   src/api/schemas/enums.ts
'   src/api/service/cases.ts
'   src/api/service/forms.ts

title Case Lifecycle - State Diagram

state NEW
state NEEDS_REVIEW
state TRIAGED
state FOLLOWING_UP
state CLOSED

[*] --> NEW
NEW --> NEEDS_REVIEW : "submitFormResponse / seekContact\n(patient active in app)"
NEW --> TRIAGED : "triageCase\n(patient not yet active)"
NEW --> CLOSED : "triageCase / contactMode=CLOSE"
NEEDS_REVIEW --> TRIAGED : "triageCase"
NEEDS_REVIEW --> CLOSED : "triageCase / contactMode=CLOSE"
TRIAGED --> FOLLOWING_UP : "advanceCaseStatus\n(Worklist: start work)"
TRIAGED --> CLOSED : "completeWorklistCase"
FOLLOWING_UP --> CLOSED : "completeWorklistCase"

note right
  VALID_TRANSITIONS enforced in
  src/api/service/cases.ts

  NEEDS_REVIEW is the patient-initiated path:
  the patient submitted a form or asked
  for contact, requiring clinician review.

  NEW → TRIAGED / CLOSED is the clinician-
  initiated path for passive patients who
  have not yet opened the app.

  triageCase is blocked while LAB/XRAY
  reviews are pending. Colleague reviews
  are advisory and never block.

  claimCaseAssignment (TRIAGED/FOLLOWING_UP)
  sets the owner without changing status.
end note

@enduml
